## Your main responsibilities

At Englobe, our health and safety culture is built on collaboration, accountability, and continuous improvement. As a Health & Safety Advisor, you will play a key role in supporting our commitment to providing a safe and healthy workplace for our employees, clients, contractors, and communities. Working closely with project teams and operational leaders throughout Atlantic Canada, you will serve as a trusted advisor, helping identify and manage risk while supporting successful project delivery. This role requires a strong field presence, sound judgment, and the ability to build productive relationships across all levels of the organization.

## Your Main Responsibilities

• Maintain a visible presence on project sites, laboratories, and operational locations throughout Atlantic Canada;

• Conduct site inspections, audits, observations, and risk assessments to identify hazards and verify compliance with safety requirements;

• Coach employees, supervisors, and project teams on hazard recognition, risk management, and safe work practices;

• Serve as a trusted advisor to operational leaders, helping prioritize health and safety risks and improvement initiatives across the region;

• Develop an understanding of Englobe's operations, project delivery models, and business objectives to help ensure health and safety programs support operational success;

• Promote and foster a positive, proactive safety culture through engagement, education, and leadership;

• Provide practical health and safety guidance to support operational objectives and successful project delivery;

• Lead or support incident investigations, root cause analyses, and the implementation of corrective and preventive actions;

• Analyze leading and lagging safety indicators, incident data, and audit findings to identify trends and improvement opportunities;

• Support the development, implementation, and continuous improvement of health and safety programs, procedures, and initiatives;

• Coordinate and participate in COR certification activities, JOHSC programs, regulatory compliance audits, and related initiatives;

• Develop and deliver safety training, orientations, toolbox talks, presentations, and awareness programs.

## What makes you unique

• Degree, diploma, or equivalent combination of education and experience in Occupational Health & Safety or a related field;

• Minimum 7-10 years of progressive health and safety experience in consulting engineering, environmental services, construction, industrial services, laboratory operations, or a related industry;

• Professional designation such as CRSP, CRST, CHSC, NCSO, or equivalent is considered an asset;

• Experience supporting both field operations and leadership teams in complex, multi-site environments;

• Strong knowledge of health and safety legislation, regulatory requirements, and industry best practices;

• Experience conducting investigations, inspections, audits, risk assessments, and corrective action management;

• Demonstrated ability to develop, implement, and maintain health and safety management systems and programs;

• Exceptional verbal and written communication skills, with the ability to engage effectively with field personnel, project teams, clients, and senior leadership.

• Valid driver's license and willingness to travel regularly throughout Atlantic Canada;

• Bilingualism (English/French) is considered an asset.

